# Project Structure

Gatsby 3 static portfolio (React 17, styled-components). Single-page home at `/`; content lives in Markdown queried at build time.

## Root

| Path | Role |
|------|------|
| `gatsby-config.js` | Plugins, `siteMetadata`, filesystem sources |
| `gatsby-node.js` | Webpack aliases; null-loaders for `scrollreveal` / `animejs` on HTML builds |
| `gatsby-browser.js` / `gatsby-ssr.js` | Client/SSR hooks |
| `src/config.js` | Site copy: email, nav links, social URLs, brand colors |
| `static/` | Files copied as-is (e.g. `og.png`) |
| `.env` | Optional secrets (see `.env.example`) |

## `src/` — application code

```
src/
├── components/     # UI; barrel export in index.js
│   ├── sections/   # Page sections (hero, about, jobs, featured, projects, contact)
│   └── icons/      # SVG icon components
├── pages/          # Gatsby routes (index.js = home)
├── styles/         # theme, GlobalStyle, mixins, fonts, Prism/transition styles
├── hooks/          # Shared React hooks (barrel: index.js)
├── images/         # Assets processed by gatsby-plugin-image / sharp
├── fonts/          # Calibre & SF Mono (woff/woff2); imported via @fonts alias
└── utils/          # Helpers (e.g. screen-reader utilities in sr.js)
```

### Path aliases (`gatsby-node.js`)

Import with `@` prefixes instead of deep relative paths:

- `@components`, `@config`, `@fonts`, `@hooks`, `@images`, `@pages`, `@styles`, `@utils`

Example:

```js
import { Layout, Hero } from '@components';
import { GlobalStyle, theme } from '@styles';
```

### Components

- **`layout.js`**: `ThemeProvider`, global shell (nav, loader, footer, optional `VirtualTwin` desktop panel).
- **`sections/*`**: One section per homepage anchor (`#about`, `#jobs`, etc.).
- **`head.js`**: SEO/meta via `react-helmet` + Gatsby `useStaticQuery`.
- Add new UI under `src/components/` and re-export from `src/components/index.js` when shared.

### Pages

- `src/pages/index.js` composes all homepage sections inside `Layout`.
- `src/pages/404.js` — not-found page.

## `content/` — Markdown data

Sourced by `gatsby-source-filesystem` + `gatsby-transformer-remark`. Frontmatter drives GraphQL in section components.

```
content/
├── jobs/<Company>/index.md    # Experience (Jobs section)
├── featured/<Slug>/          # index.md + screenshot (Featured section)
└── projects/*.md             # Project cards (Projects section)
```

### Frontmatter conventions

**Jobs** (`content/jobs/.../index.md`):

```yaml
date: '3'          # sort key (string)
title: '...'
company: '...'
location: '...'
range: '...'
url: ''            # optional company link
```

**Featured** (`content/featured/<name>/index.md` + `screenshot.png`):

```yaml
date: '2'
title: '...'
cover: './screenshot.png'
github: ''
external: ''
tech: [Node.js, React]
```

**Projects** (`content/projects/*.md`):

```yaml
date: '3'
title: '...'
github: 'https://...'
external: 'https://...'
tech: [...]
showInProjects: true   # omit or false to hide from grid
```

## Styling

- **styled-components** with shared `theme`, `mixins`, and `variables` in `src/styles/`.
- Section components typically define co-located `styled.*` blocks.
- Code blocks: Prism via `gatsby-remark-prismjs` + `PrismStyles.js`.

## Scripts

- `npm start` — `gatsby develop`
- `npm run build` / `npm run serve` — production build and preview
- `npm run format` — Prettier; pre-commit runs lint-staged (Prettier + ESLint on JS)

## Where to change things

| Goal | Location |
|------|----------|
| Nav labels / social / colors | `src/config.js` |
| New homepage section | `src/components/sections/`, wire in `pages/index.js` |
| Job / project / featured copy | `content/` Markdown |
| Site title, URL, analytics | `gatsby-config.js`, `.env` |
| Global layout or twin panel | `src/components/layout.js`, `virtualTwin.js` |
